  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nService in Cyprus\nExhibition 31 January - 29 March 2026\n\n \n\nA brand new exhibition of the sketches, photos and memories of Martin Slater, based on his National Service in the late 1950s. Now a retired lab technician, Martin Slater was educated in Oxford at the Dragon School and Magdalen College School before he spent his years of National Service with the Royal Artillery in the UK, Cyprus and later Germany, between 1956 and 1958.\n\nMartin is the author of Stranger in Saigon, a memoir from his time working with the British Medical Team in South Vitenam from 1968 - 1971.\n\nCheck the museum's opening times, dates and admission prices on our Visit Us page.\n\n \n\n \n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
